  "notes": "One of several とる verbs distinguished by kanji. {採|と}る specifically means to pick/gather from nature or to select/adopt. The kanji {採|さい} carries the sense of selecting or extracting.\n\nKANJI DISTINCTIONS (とる):\n- {取|と}る: to take (general, most common)\n- {撮|と}る: to take (photos/video)\n- {採|と}る: to gather, to pick; to adopt, to hire\n- {捕|と}る: to catch (animals, criminals)\n- {盗|と}る: to steal\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- きのこを{採|と}る: to gather mushrooms\n- {山菜|さんさい}を{採|と}る: to gather wild vegetables\n- {血液|けつえき}を{採|と}る: to draw blood\n- {多数決|たすうけつ}を{採|と}る: to take a vote\n- {人材|じんざい}を{採|と}る: to hire talent\n- {方針|ほうしん}を{採|と}る: to adopt a policy\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {取|と}る: to take (general-purpose, broadest meaning)\n- {収穫|しゅうかく}する: to harvest (agriculture, more formal)\n- {採用|さいよう}する: to adopt, to employ (formal, common in business)",
